{"title":"Career Roadmap · Leather Technologist","role":"Leather Technologist","summary":"Career positioning: Leather Technologist is a direct-entry career for a Leather Technology graduate. The role combines leather chemistry, tanning processes, material science, quality control, production engineering, product development, and increasingly, sustainability and digital manufacturing.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Leather Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"What Does a Leather Technologist Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Leather Technologist applies chemistry, materials science and manufacturing principles to convert animal hides and skins into usable leather products."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hide and skin evaluation"},{"text":"Leather processing"},{"text":"Tanning"},{"text":"Dyeing"},{"text":"Fatliquoring"},{"text":"Retanning"},{"text":"Drying"},{"text":"Finishing"},{"text":"Quality testing"},{"text":"Chemical formulation"},{"text":"Process optimisation"},{"text":"Defect analysis"},{"text":"Production control"},{"text":"Product development"},{"text":"Environmental compliance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Leather technologists can work across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tanneries"},{"text":"Leather manufacturing companies"},{"text":"Footwear companies"},{"text":"Leather-goods manufacturers"},{"text":"Automotive leather suppliers"},{"text":"Furniture/upholstery suppliers"},{"text":"Chemical companies"},{"text":"Testing laboratories"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Sustainable-material companies"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Typical Position","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech Leather Technology"},{"text":"Leather science + processing + industrial exposure"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"